       "content": "```python\ndef remove_Occ(s, char):\n    first = s.find(char)\n    last = s.rfind(char)\n    \n    if first == -1:\n        return s\n    \n    if first == last:\n        return s[:first] + s[first+1:]\n    \n    return s[:first] + s[first+1:last] + s[last+1:]\n```",
       "name": null,
       "reasoning": "The task is to write a Python function that removes the first and last occurrence of a given character from a string.\n\nLet me think about this:\n- \"hello\" with \"l\" removed: first \"l\" is at index 2, last \"l\" is at index 3. Result: \"heo\"\n\nApproach:\n1. Find the first occurrence of the character\n2. Find the last occurrence of the character\n3. Remove both occurrences\n\nI need to be careful about edge cases:\n- What if the character appears only once? Then we should remove just that one occurrence.\n- What if the character doesn't appear at all? Return the string as is.\n\nLet me write the function:\n\n```python\ndef remove_Occ(s, char):\n    first = s.find(char)\n    last = s.rfind(char)\n    \n    if first == -1:\n        return s\n    \n    if first == last:\n        return s[:first] + s[first+1:]\n    \n    return s[:first] + s[first+1:last] + s[last+1:]\n```\n\nLet me verify with the example:\n- s = \"hello\", char = \"l\"\n- first = 2, last = 3\n- s[:2] + s[3:3] + s[4:] = \"he\" + \"\" + \"o\" = \"heo\" \u2713\n\nThis looks correct.",
       "reasoning_content": "The task is to write a Python function that removes the first and last occurrence of a given character from a string.\n\nLet me think about this:\n- \"hello\" with \"l\" removed: first \"l\" is at index 2, last \"l\" is at index 3. Result: \"heo\"\n\nApproach:\n1. Find the first occurrence of the character\n2. Find the last occurrence of the character\n3. Remove both occurrences\n\nI need to be careful about edge cases:\n- What if the character appears only once? Then we should remove just that one occurrence.\n- What if the character doesn't appear at all? Return the string as is.\n\nLet me write the function:\n\n```python\ndef remove_Occ(s, char):\n    first = s.find(char)\n    last = s.rfind(char)\n    \n    if first == -1:\n        return s\n    \n    if first == last:\n        return s[:first] + s[first+1:]\n    \n    return s[:first] + s[first+1:last] + s[last+1:]\n```\n\nLet me verify with the example:\n- s = \"hello\", char = \"l\"\n- first = 2, last = 3\n- s[:2] + s[3:3] + s[4:] = \"he\" + \"\" + \"o\" = \"heo\" \u2713\n\nThis looks correct.",
